{"author":{"id":"7674679dac9170669f752d932f8b5955b1d55717359e13b1c1e687003c7bb99f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790009546,"nonce":"EDf6FMjZ4Mjn86Hsy56FUfIoleI=","title":"Task: Saved views: named query, sort and grouping in the config entity","message":"A view is a name plus a query (3c9c24d's language), a sort, a grouping and a column/field selection. Stored in the config entity alongside the schema and flows (7c90fbd), so it syncs with the tracker and merges per-key: two people adding two different views both keep them.\n\nOps: DefineView{name, spec} / RemoveView{name}. Personal vs shared is a distinction worth having early — a personal view that lives only in local storage, a shared one that lives in the entity — because everything in the entity is pushed to everyone.\n\nConsumed by: git work view (the CLI surface), the TUI's view switcher, the webui's board and list, and flow report / flow sprint, which are all really saved views with a renderer attached.","files":null}]}